    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 7 USER]\ne057\tI am leaning toward releasing an openly downloadable “workshop preview” with a fixed end date, office hours, and no compatibility promise, then deciding on the public beta after we review installation failures and the maintainer returns.\ne058\tI dislike inventing another label, and I know people can keep downloaded software after the date.\ne059\tBut I also do not want to call it a public beta when our support capacity changes halfway through.\ne060\tI have not resolved whether citations should be allowed to reference the preview.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne061\tThe proposal makes the support window and decision point concrete, but your discomfort is justified: a new label cannot fully control how released software is used.\ne062\tCitation is the unresolved commitment because it can turn a temporary preview into a durable scholarly object.\ne063\tYou could provide a citable project description without presenting the preview interface as stable, but researchers may still cite the software version they used.\ne064\tThe plan can bound your promise; it cannot make public use temporary in every practical sense.",
